From 8bd0764c020435cf431550f5921edda36684b807 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:23:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban placement: registry freshness tolerates 5 s
 Board clock skew; named machines use the same window

Closes the non-blocking nits of the independent exact-head review of PR #2100 (t_01a1d48b563e779b,
GitHub review 5889847287).

1. kanban_placement_coordination._fresh rejected any negative age (`0 <= age`). last_seen is stamped by the
   Board's clock and a just-refreshed entry's margin is sub-second (worker-7: 0.06 s), so a host whose clock
   lags the Board by ~0.1 s read a fresh machine as "from the future", i.e. stale. Since #2100 that check gates
   queue liveness (label_machines, so pool_route and queue_decision) as well as attestation (eligible). It now
   allows SKEW_S = 5 s of future skew; a stamp further ahead stays stale.
2. Docstrings (label_machines, pool_route, queue_decision) record the Board-outage behavior: wn.registry() keeps
   the last good snapshot, every entry is stale FRESH_S later, so deny-route cards go worker-first (a denied
   mandatory pin is refused) and portable cards stay local instead of queueing on pool:worker (fails closed).
3. _machine_picks_up for a named machine (heavy_route: worker-1) ignored last_seen while pool and label-set
   liveness required it. Decision: apply the same window. A machine silent past FRESH_S leases nothing (the
   Board's selection skips it), so a machine:<name> pin to it strands the card; with the window, legacy
   routing stands instead. The named branch now goes through label_machines with the empty label set, so all
   three liveness checks share one rule.

Tests: new tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_placement_freshness.py (skew rows for _fresh, label_machines,
_machine_picks_up and eligible; named-machine freshness rows; a stale heavy_route worker is not pinned).
Registry fixtures that feed named-machine heavy routing now stamp last_seen (seen_now / _machine).

Proof: RED on 45a4b03cbc (origin/main + #2100): 11 of the new tests fail (skew -0.1/-4.9 s stale, SKEW_S
missing, stale/missing last_seen named machine still picks up, stale heavy_route still pinned). GREEN on head:
the 140 test files importing the placement modules or the Board registry (3424 passed, 2 skipped).
